# CSV is the canonical tabular format, so it stays text: diffable, and a broken
# line is visible in a PR.
*.csv text
*.json text
*.md text
*.yml text

# LFS candidates. NOT enabled by default -- turning on LFS is a decision with a
# quota attached, and it should be made deliberately rather than inherited from a
# template.
#
# Before reaching for LFS, ask whether the file should be in the repository at
# all. A manifest entry's `url` field points at object storage or a facility
# archive and requires no quota, no client-side setup for collaborators, and no
# change to any downstream consumer -- the checksum is what proves the bytes are
# the same. LFS is for data that genuinely belongs with the code.
#
# To enable:  git lfs install && git lfs track "canonical/**/*.zarr/**"
# canonical/**/*.zarr/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
